daa58","maturity":"draft","page_type":"entity","path":"pages/entities/datacurve-ai-deep-swe-238be34daa58.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":[],"title":"datacurve-ai/deep-swe","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:45:11Z","updated_by_operation":"op_2c127fb00483491e87b35bfb888976ba"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_75b0561525b3a82ece80d1a6854b68c9d92d9bb998173737e7193788fc3d7f8d"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Tasks derive from upstream open-source projects under permissive licenses (e.g., MIT, Apache-2.0, BSD-3-Clause); the repo's Apache-2.0 license covers only Datacurve's original contributions, not upstream code."}],"claim_ids":["clm_75b0561525b3a82ece80d1a6854b68c9d92d9bb998173737e7193788fc3d7f8d"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T03:45:11Z","created_by_operation":"op_2c127fb00483491e87b35bfb888976ba","id":"pg_79278f4caa1057649cbaa956c770a53c","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/datacurve-ai-deep-swe-provenance-md-0b9fabbb63b9-a956c770a53c.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_196eb803adf45eca8275646a354c3c31"],"title":"datacurve-ai/deep-swe/PROVENANCE.md @ 0b9fabbb63b9","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:45:11Z","updated_by_operation":"op_2c127fb00483491e87b35bfb888976ba"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_136be139d93078e7a01a6a3da4340afd8ac1775984948462c464518f733e0261"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The benchmark comprises 113 tasks spanning TypeScript, Go, Python, JavaScript, and Rust, with isolated environments and program-based verifiers."},{"claim_ids":["clm_2fbca97b9da7abbbdbfff1842c20f3361eaf18397db44760d59072a7e2291891"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The verifier accepts any solution whose observable behavior is correct, regardless of internal symbol names or structure, and the reference patch is never used at grading time."},{"claim_ids":["clm_3bab233abd5bfce5d559362fcd663fcc102bdc351189e2f0c54bac19294f78b4"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Pier, a Harbor-compatible eval framework, adds per-agent network allowlists so agents get only needed network access while the task environment stays isolated, unlike Harbor's blanket blocking in no-internet tasks."},{"claim_ids":["clm_4e2ddcdbd7f515d20e8eda03065f1b7aaa7f47bf30f95f4f8afe97870be2bcfa"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Since v1.1, grading uses Harbor's separate verifier environment: the agent works in isolation, commits its work, and a collect hook extracts commits as a patch applied and graded in a pristine container."},{"claim_ids":["clm_4f8d0980b671bc30ae0fa074f068644e8b893ca12730f6368ec6bb70c3cba0b9"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"DeepSWE is a benchmark measuring frontier coding agents on original, long-horizon software engineering tasks drawn from active open-source repositories."},{"claim_ids":["clm_515b61b28c01e6812634967f1ccbeb0fd8d71c2f79a74584035395d6e6d7dc91"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Tasks use the Harbor task format, with task.toml metadata, instruction.md, an environment Dockerfile, tests, and a held-out reference solution."},{"claim_ids":["clm_58ecac9b533fb9cb23ab9c69e876737673c814a7041cc6c063b58809fd54316e"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Each run produces verifier outputs including reward.json with binary reward and pass fractions, ctrf.json test reports, raw stdout logs, and framework-native grader reports."},{"claim_ids":["clm_ecfb844fd722440ca026adccddf7966888d4332354a78d8cee5935bb344eac3b"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The benchmark is run via Pier, installed with uv, using commands like 'pier run -p deep-swe/tasks --agent mini-swe-agent' with model-specific API keys exported."},{"claim_ids":["clm_f21fc26059000f3bae36d300a3ca2a4c9f2d891a937f157c9ad11552d6d78c26"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Runs can be subsetted deterministically via --n-tasks with --sample-seed, or targeted at a single task by passing a task-id path to pier run."},{"claim_ids":["clm_f4bd4e999040000f03c5c6adad572761915de4b5be2b26ab519f93c7aab8a303"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The separate-verifier grading flow requires the datacurve-pier package at a version newer than 0.3.0."},{"claim_ids":["clm_ffede67f18689a3bb68db8c95fed03885addb7a11120a43100c4a8e6e3139ae8"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Pier supports multiple agents: mini-swe-agent is model-agnostic, and Pier also drives claude-code, codex, gemini-cli, and opencode; --env modal runs parallel sandboxes on Modal."}],"claim_ids":["clm_136be139d93078e7a01a6a3da4340afd8ac1775984948462c464518f733e0261","clm_2fbca97b9da7abbbdbfff1842c20f3361eaf18397db44760d59072a7e2291891","clm_3bab233abd5bfce5d559362fcd663fcc102bdc351189e2f0c54bac19294f78b4","clm_4e2ddcdbd7f515d20e8eda03065f1b7aaa7f47bf30f95f4f8afe97870be2bcfa","clm_4f8d0980b671bc30ae0fa074f068644e8b893ca12730f6368ec6bb70c3cba0b9","clm_515b61b28c01e6812634967f1ccbeb0fd8d71c2f79a74584035395d6e6d7dc91","clm_58ecac9b533fb9cb23ab9c69e876737673c814a7041cc6c063b58809fd54316e","clm_ecfb844fd722440ca026adccddf7966888d4332354a78d8cee5935bb344eac3b","clm_f21fc26059000f3bae36d300a3ca2a4c9f2d891a937f157c9ad11552d6d78c26","clm_f4bd4e999040000f03c5c6adad572761915de4b5be2b26ab519f93c7aab8a303","clm_ffede67f18689a3bb68db8c95fed03885addb7a11120a43100c4a8e6e3139ae8"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T03:45:11Z","created_by_operation":"op_2c127fb00483491e87b35bfb888976ba","id":"pg_8a0f18c4a1ba546694256d84793a8e35","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/datacurve-ai-deep-swe-readme-md-0b9fabbb63b9-6d84793a8e35.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_7d6e943246b05207a2c105d196c0044c"],"title":"datacurve-ai/deep-swe/README.md @ 0b9fabbb63b9","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:45:11Z","updated_by_operation":"op_2c127fb00483491e87b35bfb888976ba"}
